### M7.2 implementation note — jab animation and weak reaction

The jab presentation now animates the Chest bone through a short anticipation lean, forward extension/follow-through, and smooth return. Standing targets receive a brief upper-body recoil lean in addition to the existing movement impulse. `CombatPresentation.advance()` runs before the procedural arm IK updates, so the arm solver follows the animated shoulder rather than overwriting the torso pose. Host-approved wind-up/jab events already reach remote player copies, so this pose is derived locally on each peer without joint-transform streaming. Carry, limp, ragdoll and recovery continue to override combat presentation. Camera effects, strong stumble/collapse and impact VFX remain future slices.
